# systemd unit UnsetEnvironment covers only C2C_MCP_BROKER_ROOT — C2C_RELAY_CONFIG/TOKEN/IDENTITY_PATH/INSTANCES_DIR leak in

## Steps to Reproduce

1. TODO: Add steps

## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

The systemd unit UnsetEnvironment covers only C2C_MCP_BROKER_ROOT (c2c_relay_systemd.ml:110). If the user manager has imported C2C_RELAY_CONFIG (connector reads a different relay.json than the unit pin logic assumed), C2C_RELAY_TOKEN (env beats relay.json token), C2C_RELAY_IDENTITY_PATH (redirects signing identity), or C2C_INSTANCES_DIR (relocates the supervisor pidfile and singleton lock so c2c stop from a normal shell reads the home location, finds nothing, and a second connector can arm against the relocated lock), the machine connector silently misbehaves.

## Fix direction

Extend to UnsetEnvironment=C2C_MCP_BROKER_ROOT C2C_RELAY_CONFIG C2C_INSTANCES_DIR C2C_RELAY_TOKEN C2C_RELAY_IDENTITY_PATH C2C_RELAY_NODE_ID C2C_RELAY_SESSION_ID C2C_MCP_SESSION_ID; add a test pinning the list.

## Evidence

CLI review 2026-09-17 (import-environment precondition makes exploitability medium confidence; the coverage gap itself is certain).